# Kizuna core: status

Updated: 2026-11-21 · App: Mieruka · Team: Zero-Ichi

## Current state

- Django app `kizuna` is registered in `config/settings.py` and serves the landing page at `/`.
- `templates/kizuna/home.html` shows the KIZUNA 2026 hackathon logo, a header/footer and links to M1–M5.
- `views.module_page()` renders `templates/kizuna/module.html`, the shared placeholder used by every module; its logo links back home.
- `assets/kitty.png` is the site favicon. Mieruka and Zero-Ichi brand assets are in `assets/mieruka/`.
- The `kizunaserver` management command runs Django and advertises it over mDNS for the Android app (see [DEV.md](../DEV.md)).
- No business models, authentication or Mieruka feature pages are implemented.

## Documentation

- Subject and module breakdown: [k-mod/mieruka-00-index.md](../k-mod/mieruka-00-index.md)

## Changes so far

- Scaffolded the app and added the home route and shared placeholder renderer.
- Rebranded from CoRide to the Kizuna hackathon template, with header/footer module navigation.
- Refreshed the screenshots of the home page and module placeholders.

